This is a Domo Pro-Code app that is an editable table.
You have the ability to:
  add/insert/edit/remove rows with warning on remove
  add/insert/rename/remove columns
  set pagination row limit in code if desired (current set is 10,000 rows per page
  edit values in rows
  rename columns

This handles the column order and row order using a collection document containin the row and column order for you.

Set up:
Create pro-code app (I normally use the "Hello World" template
Create a collection (if you name the collection to app_table_1, you will not need to update the javascript
In the new pro-code app, add the collection to the manifest 
Add a row to the collection as "Default" and set "Sync Enabled" to "Yes"
Copy and paste the the contents of my index.html to your pro-code index.html
Copy and paste the the contents of my app.js to your pro-code app.js
Copy and paste the the contents of my app.css to your pro-code app.css
Save your pro-code app
Create a card for your pro-code app
Add the card to your created collection in "Permissions" area of the collection and give it admin access (or what ever you like.)

You can also now add your editable table to an "App Studio" app.

When you first load your app, it will provide sample columns and rows since the collection is empty. Once you add data to your collection, it will ignore the sample data.

Have fun!
